WEBVTT

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.643
one off of Western Australia
and one in the Java Trench.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:04.101
We have this wonderful ship
with a brilliant sonar.

00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:05.393
We mapped both of them.

00:05:05.417 --> 00:05:07.684
We sent landers down
to the bottom and verified.

00:05:07.708 --> 00:05:10.309
It's actually in the center portion
of the Java Trench,

00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:12.143
which is where no one thought it was.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:14.976
In fact, every time we've completed
one of our major dives,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.143
we have to run off
to Wikipedia and change it

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.643
because it's completely wrong.

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:20.309
(Laughter)

00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:23.393
DB: So it probably takes longer
to get down there

00:05:23.417 --> 00:05:25.684
than the time you're able
to spend down there?

00:05:25.708 --> 00:05:28.601
VV: No, we actually spend
quite a bit of time.

00:05:28.625 --> 00:05:31.476
I have four days
of oxygen supply in the vessel.